  grh-ln "    <div class='sb-row'><span>Hyperactivity Unified Spine</span><div class='sb-track'><div class='sb-fill ours' style='width:38.3%'></div></div><span>601 L (0 deps)</span></div>" (
  grh-ln "  </div>" (
  grh-ln "  <div class='thm-box'>" (
  grh-ln "    <div class='thm-head'><span>Initial-Algebra Universality Principle (Why 601 Lines Holds Across Every Ring)</span><span>lib/ir/poly-opt.hypercubical</span></div>" (
  grh-ln "    <p style='margin-bottom:8px'>The multivariate polynomial ring <span class='m'>&Zopf;[<i>x</i><sub>0</sub>, &hellip;, <i>x</i><sub><i>n</i>&minus;1</sub>]</span> is the <strong>initial object</strong> in the category of commutative rings equipped with an <span class='m'><i>n</i></span>-tuple of elements: for every commutative ring <span class='m'><i>R</i> &isin; {&Zopf;, &Qopf;, &Ropf;, &Copf;, &Zopf;<sub>&#x2113;</sub>, &Aopf;<sub><i>F</i></sub>}</span> and every assignment <span class='m'><i>a</i> : {0..<i>n</i>&minus;1} &rarr; <i>R</i></span>, there exists a unique ring homomorphism <span class='m'>ev<sub><i>a</i></sub> : &Zopf;[<i>X</i>] &rarr; <i>R</i></span>.</p>" (
  grh-ln "    <p style='margin-bottom:0'>When <code>PolyOptCert</code> proves <code>re-norm-ok n spec cand &equiv; true</code> by interaction-net normalization (<code>refl</code>), equality in <span class='m'><i>R</i></span> holds functorially without constructing Cauchy reals, <span class='m'>&#x2113;</span>-adic limits, or classical quotients—and lowers directly to 0-DRC silicon and zero-UB C11.</p>" (
  grh-ln "  </div>" nil)))))))))))))))))))))))))))
